  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- number of jobs created 
- illiteracy rate
- vocational trainings</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2013">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- illiteracy
- lack of vocational training 
- unemployment</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Ready Made Garments (RMG) factory 
- Number of beneficiaries of the vocational training 
- Number of jobs created 
- Number of beneficiaries of illiteracy classes</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2020, 1,712 beneficiaries in which around 25 % are women received training through ENID and created 590 job opportunities in which 72% are women. In addition as a response to COVID-19 ENID shifted the activity of the RMG factory in Qena to the production of medical masks to meet the high demand in Qena and created 119 jobs and training for 102 women beneficiaries on the production of masks</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Raise the capacity of 445 beneficiaries

&#x2022;	Ready Made Garments (RMG) factory is fully Operational and production increased.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	ENID has trained 445 females from 7 villages on sewing basics and the operation of both single and overlock sewing machines. 
&#x2022;	The beneficiaries received training on drape&#x2019;s, stiches and gophers, as well as kids&#x2019; dresses, T-shirts and bedsheets. 

&#x2022;	The factory building is rented and renovated
&#x2022;	The factory is fully furnished and ready to be operational. Factory necessary equipment and machinery are purchased according to specification. (37 textiles machines have been purchased for the whole factory as well as one embroidery machine with 12 heads is purchased with an amount of EGP 600,000)
&#x2022;	200 Women from villages in Qous District namely Abasa, Geziret Motteira, Makhzan, Haragueia and Kharanka received cut and sew training and those qualified will be selected to start working at the factory.
&#x2022;	Factory Admin staff are chosen
&#x2022;	Initial agreements with off takers are put in place for the purpose of exporting all the products of the factory.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Raise the capacity of 638 beneficiaries on agriculture and sewing and also train them to work in Ready Made Garments (RMG ) Factory on the production of masks. 
&#x2022;	Creation of 500 job opportunity in the area of agriculture, handicrafts, wood, furniture and production of masks.
&#x2022;	 25 illiteracy classes which will enable them to be enrolled in the vocational training and then be qualified to secure a job.
&#x2022;	Ready Made Garments (RMG) factory is operational, and production increased</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	ENID project raised the capacity of 670 beneficiaries on agriculture and sewing and also train them to work in Ready Made Garments (RMG ) Factory on the production of masks.
&#x2022;	ENID project created 227 job opportunity in the area in the area of agriculture, handicrafts, wood, furniture and production of masks.
&#x2022;	25 illiteracy classes which enable them to be enrolled in the vocational training and then be qualified to secure a job.
&#x2022;	Production of masks factory is operational, and production increased</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
